      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/4/25/18",
      "text": [
        " اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : \"قِيلَ لِعِيسَى اِبْنِ مَرْيَمَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ مَا لَكَ لاَ تَتَزَوَّجُ فَقَالَ وَ مَا أَصْنَعُ بِالتَّزْوِيجِ قَالُوا يُولَدُ لَكَ قَالَ وَ مَا أَصْنَعُ بِالْأَوْلاَدِ إِنْ عَاشُوا فَتَنُوا وَ إِنْ مَاتُوا أَحْزَنُوا\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4916 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) said:\n\"It was said to Isa (as) (Jesus), the son of Mariyum {s.a} (Mary): 'Why do you not marry?'\nIsa (as) replied: 'And what would I do with marriage?'\nThey said: 'Children would be born to you.'\nIsa (as) said: 'And what would I do with children? If they live, they will lead to trials, and if they die, they will cause me sorrow.'\""
        ]
      }
    },
